.Dd $Mdocdate: November 5 2026 $
.Dt SIGNET-API 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm signet-api
.Nd signet HTTP API
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr signet 1
listens for HTTP on
.Va listen
.Pq default Pa :8080 ,
a TCP address or, when it is an absolute path, a Unix domain socket —
usually behind a TLS-terminating reverse proxy; see
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5 .
.Pp
Requests are logged one line each at the
.Dq info
level:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
http request method=POST uri="/login" status=200 bytes=41 duration=312us remote=192.0.2.9
.Ed
.Pp
The client address is the connection's, or, from a peer in
.Li trusted_proxies ,
the rightmost
.Ev X-Forwarded-For
entry that is not a trusted proxy.
.Pp
Every refused attempt is also logged as a warning naming the limit:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
WARN: rate limited: login attempts for a@example.com from 192.0.2.9
WARN: rate limited: PIN send for a@example.com from 192.0.2.9
WARN: rate limited: validation API for client "scribe" from 192.0.2.9
.Ed
.Sh CONVENTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Paths
The paths below are from the root.
With
.Li base_path
set, every one is under it:
.Pa /login
is then
.Pa /comments-auth/login .
Outside the base everything answers
.Sy 404 .
Redirects and links name the base, the default return address after a sign-in
.Pa /comments-auth/account
included.
.It Limits
A request body over 128 KiB answers
.Sy 413 .
Every response carries
.Li X-Frame-Options: DENY
and
.Li X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff .
What is not a valid address is refused before anything else looks at it.
An address is one plain
.Li local@domain :
lists, names, quotes, comments,
.Li \&|
and
.Li /
are refused.
Addresses match without regard to case, and replies, sessions and
.Li Remote-Email
give the account's own form.
.It Cross-origin requests
A browser's request other than
.Li GET ,
.Li HEAD
or
.Li OPTIONS
from another origin answers
.Sy 403
.Li {"success":false,"error":"Cross-origin request refused"} ,
unless its host is in
.Li allowed_redirect_hosts .
The browser's
.Li Sec-Fetch-Site
header decides; without it,
.Li Origin
must match
.Li Host ,
so a web server in front must pass
.Li Host
on unchanged.
Clients that send neither header are not affected.
.Li /api/v1/validate
is exempt: its API key and each client's
.Li allowed_origins
govern it.
.It Content types
Request bodies are JSON
.Pq Li application/json
except the login and recovery forms.
Responses are JSON on the API endpoints, and
.Li text/plain
for endpoints that do not negotiate.
.It Content negotiation
.Cm POST /login
answers JSON when the request carries
.Li Accept: application/json
or
.Li X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest ,
and a redirect otherwise.
.It Authentication
Everything except
.Cm GET /login ,
.Cm POST /login ,
.Cm GET /recover ,
.Cm POST /recover ,
.Cm GET /register ,
.Cm POST /register ,
.Cm GET /health
and the WebAuthn/PIN entry points requires the session cookie
.Va signetid .
.It Errors
Every JSON endpoint answers failures with a JSON body and an HTTP status code
that describes the failure, so a client can branch on the status alone.
The body is
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"success": false, "error": "human readable reason"}
.Ed
for actions, and
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"valid": false, "error": "human readable reason"}
.Ed
for
.Cm /session
and
.Cm /api/v1/validate .
Plain-text bodies remain only on the HTML form paths
.Pq Cm POST /login No without JSON negotiation , Cm GET /login .
.El
.Sh SESSIONS
A successful sign-in creates a row in the session store and sets a cookie:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Set-Cookie: signetid=<token>:<signature>; Path=/; Max-Age=86400;
    HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict[; Secure]
.Ed
.Pp
The value is a random token, 32 bytes as 64 hex characters, and a signature:
the SHA-256 of
.Va cookie_secret
followed by the token, in hex.
It is not an HMAC, and needs none: each token is also looked up in the
session store, so a signature alone admits nobody.
Sessions survive a restart, and instances sharing a database accept each
other's cookies when they use the same secret.
Changing the secret signs everyone out.
.Va Secure
is controlled by
.Va cookie_secure
and
.Va Max-Age
by
.Va cookie_max_age ,
or for a RADIUS account by the reply's
.Li Session-Timeout .
With
.Va session_idle_timeout
set, a session no request has read for that long ends, and
.Cm GET /session
answers
.Li "session expired" ;
.Cm GET /session ,
.Cm POST /api/v1/validate
and the account page count as a use, written down at most once a minute.
.Pp
.Cm GET /session
also returns the headers
.Ev Remote-User
and
.Ev Remote-Email ,
and
.Ev Remote-Avatar
for an account with a picture,
so a reverse proxy can use it for forward authentication.
A visitor can send these headers too.
The proxy must remove the visitor's copies of all three before the request
reaches the application, since
.Ev Remote-Avatar
is not always replaced.
.Sh ENDPOINTS
.Ss Login
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm GET /login
Renders the login page
.Pq Pa login.html ,
honouring
.Cm ?referrer= .
An unencoded value with a
.Sq \&?
of its own, as a web server sends, is taken whole and verbatim, to the end of
the query.
Answers
.Sy 200
with HTML.
.It Cm POST /login
Form-encoded with
.Va email ,
.Va password
and optionally
.Va referrer .
With
.Va radius.enabled ,
.Va email
may be a plain name, and a name the CSV file lacks is checked by the RADIUS
servers; see
.Sx RADIUS accounts .
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Sy 200
JSON
.Li {"success":true,"redirect":"/path"}
plus the session cookie.
.It Sy 302
Location set to the same target, plus the cookie.
.It Sy 400
email or password missing.
.It Sy 401
invalid credentials, an unknown, locked or unapproved account, the address
is rate limited, or the account is locked after
.Va account_lockout_threshold
failed sign-ins in a row, right password or not, always with the same answer.
.It Sy 403
.Va auth_methods.password
is disabled, or the claims hook refused under
.Li fail-closed .
.It Sy 500
the page could not be rendered.
.It Sy 503
no RADIUS server gave a valid reply, for a name the CSV file lacks.
.El
.Pp
The redirect target is, in order, the posted
.Va referrer ,
the
.Cm ?referrer=
query parameter, the HTTP
.Ev Referer
header, then the account page
.Pa /account .
Only local paths and URLs on the same host are accepted,
plus absolute URLs on hosts listed in
.Va allowed_redirect_hosts
.Pq see Xr signet-config.yaml 5 ,
which are returned in full.
A path with a
.Li \&.
or
.Li \&..
segment, encoded or not, is refused, since a browser resolves
.Pa /.//evil.example/
to
.Pa //evil.example/ ,
another host.
This instance's
.Pa /login ,
.Pa /register ,
.Pa /recover
and
.Pa /logout
are never a target: returning to one after registering confuses, and to
.Pa /logout
signs the person out again.
.It Cm GET /
With a session, HTML naming the signed-in user.
Without one,
.Sy 302
to
.Pa /login .
.El
.Ss Session
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm GET /session
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Sy 200
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"valid":true, "user":..., "email":..., "method":...,
 "created_at":..., "expires_at":..., "claims":{...},
 "claims_refreshed":false, "avatar":null}
.Ed
and the
.Ev Remote-User
header, and
.Ev Remote-Email
when the account is a mail address.
A RADIUS account named
.Li jdoe
has
.Li "email":""
and no
.Ev Remote-Email .
.Li method
is
.Li password ,
.Li email_pin ,
.Li webauthn
or
.Li radius ,
followed by
.Li +
and the second step when there was one.
.Li avatar
is the URL of the account's picture, or
.Li null
when it has none or
.Va avatars
is off; when it is set, the
.Ev Remote-Avatar
header has the same value.
.It Sy 401
.Li {"valid":false,"error":"..."}
for an absent, expired or forged cookie.
.El
.Pp
.Cm ?claims=refresh
re-runs the external claims hook, stores its answer and returns it with
.Li "claims_refreshed":true .
An account gets
.Va claims_hook.refresh_rate_limit
runs in
.Va claims_hook.refresh_rate_window
seconds; past that the stored claims are answered with
.Li "claims_refreshed":false ,
as when the hook fails.
Without a configured hook the parameter does nothing.
For a RADIUS account the hook is given the reply stored at sign-in.
.It Cm GET /logout , Cm POST /logout
Deletes the session row and expires the cookie
.Pq Li Max-Age=0 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Sy 200
.Li {"success":true}
for XHR requests.
.It Sy 303
to
.Pa /login
otherwise.
.It Sy 405
any other method.
.El
.Pp
Logging out without a session succeeds the same way.
.El
.Ss Recovery
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm GET /recover
Renders
.Pa recover.html ,
with
.Li .RecoveryEnabled
true when
.Va password_recovery
is enabled,
.Va public_url
is set and passwords are not disabled.
A mailed link is
.Li <public_url><base_path>/recover#token=<token> ,
and the page's script checks it before asking for a password.
.Sy 200 .
.It Cm POST /recover
Form-encoded.
.Sy 403
when recovery is off.
With
.Li email :
.Sy 400
without one, otherwise
.Sy 200
and the same text for every address, and a link is mailed if the account may
sign
in.
With
.Li token :
.Sy 200
if the link is live,
.Sy 400
if not, and nothing is spent.
With
.Li token
and
.Li password :
.Sy 400
for a dead link or a short password, which leaves the link usable, otherwise
.Sy 200 ;
the password changes, every session of the account ends and a notice is mailed.
With
.Li Accept: application/json
replies are
.Li {"success":...,"message":...}
or
.Li "error" .
.El
.Ss Code step
For an account with a TOTP key, a right password or PIN starts no session.
.Cm POST /login
answers the page with its code form, or with
.Li Accept: application/json ,
.Li {"success":false,"totp_required":true,"step":"code","pending":"..."} ,
and
.Cm POST /email-pin/verify
answers that JSON.
.Cm POST /login
with form fields
.Li pending
and
.Li code ,
which may be a recovery code, then answers
.Sy 302
and the session cookie, or
.Sy 401
and the page.
A code works once, five wrong ones per address in five minutes stop further
tries, and
.Li pending
lasts five minutes.
The session's
.Li method
says what was used, such as
.Dq password+totp .
.Pp
With
.Va second_factor
.Dq required ,
every sign-in by password or PIN takes a second step, named in the JSON
.Li step :
.Dq code ,
.Dq mail
or
.Dq enrol ;
.Li totp_required
is true only for the first.
A security key must verify its user and signs in alone.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dq mail
After a password, with
.Li email_pin
in
.Va second_factor_methods ,
a PIN is mailed;
.Li pending
and
.Li code
set to it answer as above.
A wrong PIN counts toward the lockout, and after three the step ends.
.It Dq enrol
For an account with no app and no key,
.Li pending
and
.Li action :
none shows the choices;
.Li totp-begin
shows a new app key;
.Li totp-finish
with
.Li code
answers
.Sy 200 ,
the session and the recovery codes, once;
.Li key
answers
.Sy 303
to
.Pa /webauthn/keys
with a one-time invite in the fragment, after which the key signs in.
The step lasts fifteen minutes.
.El
.Pp
An account whose only second factor is a key gets
.Sy 403
for a right password or PIN.
.Cm POST /account
refuses with
.Sy 409
to remove an account's last app or key, unless
.Va second_factor_methods
lists
.Li email_pin .
.Ss RADIUS accounts
With
.Va radius.enabled ,
a password for a name the CSV file does not have is checked by the RADIUS
servers
.Pq Xr signet-config.yaml 5 .
A name the file has never goes to them, so a local account shadows a RADIUS one
of the same name.
.Nm signet Cm session-revoke
ends a RADIUS account's sessions.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Access-Accept
As a password: the session's
.Li method
is
.Li radius ,
and its claims are
.Li {"groups":[...]} ,
or the claims hook's answer
.Pq Xr signet-hooks 5 .
An authenticator app's code may follow
.Pq Li radius+totp .
A
.Li Session-Timeout
sets the session's lifetime and the cookie's
.Li Max-Age ,
and an
.Li Idle-Timeout
its idle limit, each up to
.Va radius.max_session_timeout
and
.Va radius.max_idle_timeout .
.It Access-Challenge
No session.
JSON gets
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"success":false,"step":"radius","pending":"...",
 "message":"the server's Reply-Message"}
.Ed
and a form gets the page asking for it.
.Cm POST /login
with
.Va pending
and
.Va code
set to the answer sends it, with the challenge's
.Li State ,
to the server that asked.
One answer spends the step, which lasts five minutes; a sign-in answers at most
three challenges.
.It Access-Reject
.Sy 401 ,
counted as a failed sign-in.
.It No reply
.Sy 503 ,
not counted against the account.
.El
.Pp
A RADIUS account has no password, PIN, recovery, registration or security key
here; each answers as for an unknown address.
With
.Va second_factor
.Dq required
it takes only the
.Dq code
or
.Dq enrol
step, and adds only an app.
.Pa /account
shows its apps and picture, and refuses a password change with
.Sy 403 .
.Ss Account
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm GET /account
Renders
.Pa account.html ,
or
.Sy 302
to
.Pa /login
with no session.
.It Cm POST /account
JSON.
.Li {"action":"password","current":"...","new":"..."}
changes the password, ends the account's other sessions and mails a notice.
.Sy 401
with no session,
.Sy 403
when the sign-in is older than
.Va account_reauth_window ,
.Sy 400
for a wrong current password or a short new one.
.Pp
With TOTP on,
.Li {"action":"totp-begin","label":"..."}
answers
.Li secret ,
.Li url
and
.Li qr ,
a PNG data URI, and saves nothing.
.Li {"action":"totp-finish","code":"..."}
saves the key if the code is right, answering
.Li recovery_codes
for an account's first key.
.Li {"action":"totp-remove","id":"..."}
removes a key and ends the account's other sessions.
.Li {"action":"totp-codes"}
replaces the recovery codes.
.Pp
With
.Va avatars
on,
.Li {"action":"avatar-set","image":"..."}
stores a picture: a PNG or JPEG, base64, exactly
.Va avatar_size
pixels square, answering its path as
.Li avatar .
.Sy 400
for another size or format,
.Sy 429
past
.Va avatar_rate_limit .
.Li {"action":"avatar-remove"}
removes it.
Neither mails a notice.
.It Cm GET /avatar/<id>
The picture, to anyone, with
.Li Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable .
The id is random and new with every upload;
.Sy 404
once the picture is replaced or removed.
It is never served as uploaded: it is decoded and encoded again, which drops
metadata.
.El
.Pp
Adding or removing a security key needs a recent sign-in too, and answers
.Sy 403
without one, unless an invite is used.
.Ss Email PIN
Both endpoints answer
.Sy 503
when
.Va auth_methods.email_pin
is not enabled.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm POST /email-pin/send
JSON
.Li {"email": "a@example.com"} .
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Sy 200
.Li {"success":true,"message":"PIN sent to your email"}
.It Sy 400
malformed body or missing address.
.It Sy 429
rate limit exceeded, per requester or per address.
.It Sy 500
an internal error, such as the database being unavailable.
.El
The
.Sy 200
is the same for every address: no mail goes to an unknown account, one that may
not sign in, or one locked out after wrong guesses,
and a message the mail system
refuses also answers
.Sy 200 .
.It Cm POST /email-pin/verify
JSON
.Li {"email": "a@example.com", "pin": "123456"} .
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Sy 200
.Li {"success":true,"message":"PIN verified successfully"}
and the session cookie.
.It Sy 400
missing fields, or the PIN is wrong, used or expired.
Three wrong guesses against an address lock PIN sign-in for it for 30 minutes,
with the same answer, whichever client address made them.
.It Sy 403
the claims hook refused under
.Li fail-closed .
.It Sy 429
rate limit exceeded.
.It Sy 500
internal error.
.El
.El
.Ss WebAuthn
Bodies are JSON in the WebAuthn Level 2 encoding, with binary fields base64url
encoded.
A
.Sy start
call returns a
.Li ceremony
ID, which the matching
.Sy finish
call presents once; it expires after five minutes.
Enrollment acts on the account of the signed-in session, or of the invite in
the
.Li X-Signet-Invite
header; an address in the request is ignored.
The calls that start or finish a ceremony count against
.Li webauthn_rate_limit
per requester, and over budget answer
.Sy 429
with
.Li {"success":false,"error":"Rate limit exceeded"} .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm GET /webauthn/invite
With the invite in the
.Li X-Signet-Invite
header, whether it can still enroll a key, without spending it.
.Sy 200
.Li {"success":true} ,
.Sy 400
without an invite,
.Sy 401
when it is used, expired or unknown,
.Sy 403
when the account may not sign in.
.It Cm POST /webauthn/register/start
.Sy 200
.Li {"success":true,"options":{...},"ceremony":"..."} ,
.Sy 401
without a session or valid invite,
.Sy 403
when the account may not sign in.
.It Cm POST /webauthn/register/finish?ceremony=...&label=...
Body: the registration response.
.Sy 200
.Li {"success":true,"credential":{...}} ,
.Sy 400
when it fails verification,
.Sy 401
and
.Sy 403
as above.
Using an invite spends it.
.It Cm POST /webauthn/authenticate/start?email=...
.Sy 200
.Li {"success":true,"options":{...},"ceremony":"..."} ,
.Sy 400
without an address.
.Sy 401
for what is not a valid address.
Any valid address gets options, so the reply does not show which accounts have a
key: one that is unknown, may not sign in or has no keys is offered invented
keys
that stay the same for that address, and finishing fails.
.It Cm POST /webauthn/authenticate/finish?email=...&ceremony=...
Body: the assertion response.
.Sy 200
.Li {"success":true}
and the session cookie,
.Sy 401
when it fails verification or the signature counter did not increase,
.Sy 403
when the claims hook refuses under
.Li fail-closed .
.It Cm GET /webauthn/credentials
The signed-in user's credentials,
.Sy 401
without a session.
.It Cm DELETE /webauthn/credentials/<id>
Delete one of the signed-in user's credentials and end every session of the
account, this one included.
.Sy 200
.Li {"success":true,"signed_out":true}
and the session cookie expired,
.Sy 404
when no such credential belongs to them.
.It Cm GET /webauthn/keys
The security-key page.
An invite link opens it with
.Li #invite=...
in the fragment.
.El
.Ss Validation API
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm POST /api/v1/validate
For applications registered with
.Cm signet client-add ,
which prints the key once.
The key travels in the
.Li X-API-Key
header.
The
.Va signetid
cookie may be sent in the
.Li Cookie
header, or in the JSON body as
.Li {"cookie": "..."}
\(em the body wins when both are present, so an application that stores the
value itself does not depend on the caller's headers.
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Sy 200
.Li {"valid":true,"user":...,"method":...,"claims":{...},"avatar":...}
.It Sy 400
the JSON body is not valid JSON.
.It Sy 401
.Li {"valid":false,"error":"..."}
for a missing or unknown API key, a missing cookie, a bad signature, or a
session that has expired or been deleted.
.It Sy 403
a CORS preflight from an origin no client allows.
.It Sy 405
any method but POST.
.It Sy 429
.Li {"valid":false,"error":"rate limit exceeded"}
above
.Va api_rate_limit
per
.Va api_rate_window .
.El
.Pp
When the request carries an
.Li Origin
allowed by a client's
.Va allowed_origins ,
the response adds the matching CORS headers, and
.Cm OPTIONS
answers
.Sy 204 .
.El
.Ss Miscellaneous
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm GET /health
.Sy 200
.Li {"status":"ok"} .
.It Cm GET /static/js/webauthn.js
The browser WebAuthn client, when
.Va static_dir
is set.
Only files are served from
.Va static_dir :
a directory answers
.Sy 404
and is never listed.
.It Cm GET /register
Renders
.Pa register.html .
.It Cm POST /register
.Sy 403
while registration is off.
With
.Va email_verification
.Dq required ,
form field
.Li email
answers
.Sy 200
and the same text for every address, and mails a link, or tells the owner of an
account that it exists;
.Li token
checks a link, spending nothing;
.Li token
and
.Li password
create the account, or answer
.Sy 400
for a dead link, an address that now has an account or a short password.
An account never exists before its link is used.
With
.Va email_verification
.Dq disabled ,
.Li email
and
.Li password
create it at once and answer
.Sy 302 ,
.Sy 409
when the address has an account, and
.Sy 429
over
.Li register_rate_limit
per requester.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign in and keep the cookie:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -c jar -H 'Accept: application/json' \e
    -d 'email=a@example.com&password=secret&referrer=/app' \e
    http://127.0.0.1:8080/login
{"redirect":"/app","success":true}
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect the session:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -b jar http://127.0.0.1:8080/session
{"valid":true,"user":"a@example.com","method":"password",...}
.Ed
.Pp
Sign out:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -b jar -X POST -H 'Accept: application/json' \e
    http://127.0.0.1:8080/logout
{"success":true}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr signet 1 ,
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5 ,
.Xr signet-hooks 5 ,
.Xr signet-template 5
.Sh CAVEATS
.Cm POST /email-pin/send
answers
.Sy 200
whether or not a message was handed to the mail system, so that it shows nothing
about which accounts exist.
A refusal is in the log.
.Pp
Removing an account from the CSV file by hand, or setting its
.Dq locked
flag, stops new logins but leaves existing sessions valid until they expire;
.Cm signet user-delete
ends them.
.Pp
An API client's key is shown once by
.Cm signet client-add ;
store it in the application's configuration.
Deleting the client with
.Cm signet client-revoke
invalidates the key immediately.
